    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini-files\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nThe go_in function in mini.files replaces the buffer in the most recent window now. Can an option to open the file in horizontal/vertical split of the most recent window also be added? The key-bindings 'S' and 'V' can be set by default for this. This will simplify opening files side by side.\r\nAlso this can be done by a custom config using existing apis, but I think it would be good to have this builtin by default.\r\n",
